Authorization subscriptions in the SAPL binary format, as the RSocket API receives them on a
connection with the data MIME type application/vnd.sapl.binary.

The format is specified in BINARY_FORMAT.md of this crate. A payload is the lead byte 00, which
is the version of the format, the length of the text region, the region with all texts in UTF-8,
and the structure: subject, action, resource, environment and secrets, one value each. A value is
one tag byte, followed by what the tag needs; a text names the next bytes of the region. The
secrets must be an object. Nothing may follow, and every byte of the region must belong to a text.
Arrays and objects nest at most 500 deep, the secrets object at depth 1. A number beyond the
limits of the value model refuses the payload.

The document is the payload in hexadecimal bytes. A '//' starts a comment to the end of the line.
The expectation is either the five parts, each as JSON or as the word 'undefined' or 'error', or
'refused' with the reason.

=== three short texts, no environment and no secrets
00 0c 61 6c 69 63 65 72 65 61 64 64 6f 63   // region "alicereaddoc"
25 24 23                                  // "alice" "read" "doc"
00                                        // environment undefined
60                                        // secrets {}
---
subject: "alice"
action: "read"
resource: "doc"
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== a subscription with all five parts
00 16 61 6c 69 63 65 72 65 61 64 69 64 74 6f 6b 65 6e 73 33 63 72 33 74   // region
25                // subject "alice"
24                // action "read"
61 02 87          // resource {"id":7}
01                // environment null
61 05 26          // secrets {"token":"s3cr3t"}
---
subject: "alice"
action: "read"
resource: {"id":7}
environment: null
secrets: {"token":"s3cr3t"}

=== values of every kind that JSON has
00 08 78 72 65 61 64 61 62 63   // region "xreadabc"
47 01 03 02                     // subject: 7 elements, null, true, false,
   05 fa 01 02                  //   12.5 as 125 with scale 1,
   21 40 60                     //   "x", [], {}
24                              // action "read"
62 01 21 01 41 81               // resource {"a":"b","c":[1]}
00 60
---
subject: [null,true,false,12.5,"x",[],{}]
action: "read"
resource: {"a":"b","c":[1]}
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== the long forms of texts, arrays, objects and integers
00 06 61 6c 69 63 65 61         // region "alicea"
08 05                           // subject: text of 5 bytes
09 01 04 02                     // action: array of 1 element, the integer 1
0a 01 01 04 02                  // resource: object of 1 entry, "a": 1
04 00                           // environment: the integer 0
0a 00                           // secrets: object of no entries
---
subject: "alice"
action: [1]
resource: {"a":1}
environment: 0
secrets: {}

=== numbers: integers, decimals and a big decimal
00 05 72 65 61 64 78            // region "readx"
4a                              // subject, an array of 10 elements:
   04 01                        //   -1
   ff                           //   127
   04 80 02                     //   128
   04 fe ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff 01   // the largest 64-bit integer
   04 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff 01   // the smallest 64-bit integer
   05 f4 03 04                  //   2.50 as 250 with scale 2
   05 02 cf 0f                  //   1e1000 as 1 with scale -1000
   e4                           //   100
   06 00 09 05 6b c7 5e 2d 63 10 00 00   // 100000000000000000000, beyond 64 bits
   05 09 02                     //   -0.5 as -5 with scale 1
24 21 00 60
---
subject: [-1,127,128,9223372036854775807,-9223372036854775808,2.50,1e1000,100,100000000000000000000,-0.5]
action: "read"
resource: "x"
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== a whole decimal is the integer it denotes
00 00
05 c8 01 04                     // 100 with scale 2
05 00 00                        // 0 with scale 0
05 01 00                        // -1 with scale 0
00 60
---
subject: 1
action: 0
resource: -1
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== a decimal at the limit of the scale
00 00
05 02 d0 0f                     // 1 with scale 1000
05 02 cf 0f                     // 1 with scale -1000
00 00 60
---
subject: 1e-1000
action: 1e1000
resource: undefined
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== undefined and an error
00 05 42 6f 6f 6d 2e            // region "Boom."
00                              // subject undefined
07 05                           // action, an error with the message "Boom."
01 00 60
---
subject: undefined
action: error
resource: null
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== a key authored twice keeps its first position and the last value
00 03 61 62 61                  // region "aba", the keys in order
00 00
63 01 81 01 82 01 83            // resource {"a":1,"b":2,"a":3}
00 60
---
subject: undefined
action: undefined
resource: {"a":3,"b":2}
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== characters outside ASCII
00 06 c3 a9 f0 9f 98 80         // region
26                              // subject, a text of 6 bytes
00 00 00 60
---
subject: "<U+00E9><U+1F600>"
action: undefined
resource: undefined
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== an empty text and an empty key
00 00
20                              // subject ""
61 00 01                        // action {"":null}
00 00 60
---
subject: ""
action: {"":null}
resource: undefined
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== arrays nested to the limit
00 00 <499 times 41 >40 00 00 00 60
---
subject: <499 times [>[]<499 times ]>
action: undefined
resource: undefined
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== objects nested to the limit
00 00 <500 times 61 00 >81 00 00 00 60
---
subject: <500 times {"":>1<500 times }>
action: undefined
resource: undefined
environment: undefined
secrets: {}

=== arrays nested beyond the limit
00 00 <501 times 41 >81 00 00 00 60
---
refused: too deep

=== an empty array nested beyond the limit
00 00 <500 times 41 >40 00 00 00 60
---
refused: too deep

=== secrets nested to the limit, the secrets object at depth 1
00 00 00 00 00 00 61 00 <499 times 41 >81
---
subject: undefined
action: undefined
resource: undefined
environment: undefined
secrets: {"":<499 times [>1<499 times ]>}

=== secrets nested beyond the limit
00 00 00 00 00 00 61 00 <500 times 41 >81
---
refused: too deep

=== the empty payload
---
refused: malformed

=== only the lead byte
00
---
refused: malformed

=== a payload without the lead byte
0c 61 6c 69 63 65 72 65 61 64 64 6f 63 25 24 23 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a lead byte of another version
01 0c 61 6c 69 63 65 72 65 61 64 64 6f 63 25 24 23 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a protobuf subscription, whose first byte is a field key
0a 07 22 05 61 6c 69 63 65 12 06 22 04 72 65 61 64 1a 05 22 03 64 6f 63
---
refused: malformed

=== cut off after the subject
00 00 81
---
refused: malformed

=== cut off inside a varint
00 00 04 80
---
refused: malformed

=== a region longer than the payload
00 05 61 62
---
refused: malformed

=== a region that is not UTF-8
00 01 ff 21 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a surrogate encoded in UTF-8
00 03 ed a0 80 23 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== an overlong encoding in UTF-8
00 02 c0 af 22 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a text that ends inside a character
00 02 c3 a9 21 21 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a text beyond the region
00 01 61 22 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== bytes of the region that belong to no text
00 02 61 62 21 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a byte after the secrets
00 00 00 00 00 00 60 00
---
refused: malformed

=== an unknown tag
00 00 0b 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== the last unknown tag
00 00 1f 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== an array with more elements than the payload has bytes
00 00 09 ff ff ff ff 0f 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== an object with more entries than the payload has bytes
00 00 7f 00 81
---
refused: malformed

=== a varint of eleven bytes
00 00 04 80 80 80 80 80 80 80 80 80 80 01 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a varint beyond 64 bits
00 00 04 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff 02 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a text length beyond the region
00 00 08 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff 01 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a decimal with a scale beyond the limit
00 00 05 02 d2 0f 00 00 00 60   // 1 with scale 1001
---
refused: invalid number

=== a decimal with a negative scale beyond the limit
00 00 05 02 d1 0f 00 00 00 60   // 1 with scale -1001
---
refused: invalid number

=== a big decimal of no bytes
00 00 06 00 00 00 00 00 60
---
refused: invalid number

=== a big decimal of more bytes than a number of 1000 digits needs
00 00 06 00 a3 03 <419 times 01 > 00 00 00 60
---
refused: invalid number

=== secrets that are a number
00 00 00 00 00 00 81
---
refused: secrets not an object

=== secrets that are an array
00 00 00 00 00 00 40
---
refused: secrets not an object

=== secrets that are null
00 00 00 00 00 00 01
---
refused: secrets not an object

=== no secrets at all
00 00 00 00 00 00
---
refused: malformed
